import Polyfold.Chapter2.LevelPolyfold

/-!
Hofer–Wysocki–Zehnder, *Polyfold and Fredholm Theory I* (2014 preprint), Part I, §2.2,
Definitions 2.17–2.18, Proposition 2.3.15 (preprint 2.19) and the paragraph after it (the tangent bundle `TX` of an
M-polyfold), with the tangent functor of §2.1 (the paragraph after Theorem 2.1.15 (preprint 2.8)) made explicit.

# The tangent bundle `TX → X¹` of an M-polyfold

## The text, paraphrased

(Definition 2.1.12 (preprint 2.5)) `T(O, C, E) = (TO, TC, TE)` with `TC = C¹ ⊕ E` a partial quadrant in
`TE = E¹ ⊕ E`, `TU` relatively open in `TC`, and `TO = Tr(TU)`.  (After Theorem 2.1.15 (preprint 2.8)) `T` is a
functor: `Tf : (TO, TC, TE) → (TO', TC', TE')`, `T(g ∘ f) = Tg ∘ Tf`.  (Definition 2.3.12 (preprint 2.17)) `T_xO =
p⁻¹(x)` for `x ∈ O₁`, where `p : TO → O₁`; `T_xO = Dr(x)E`.  Tuples `(x, V, φ, (O, C, E), h)`,
`x ∈ X₁`, `φ` a chart around `x`, `h ∈ T_{φ(x)}O`, are equivalent if the points agree and
`T(φ ∘ ψ⁻¹)(ψ(x)) h' = h`.  (Definition 2.3.14 (preprint 2.18)) `TX` is the set of equivalence classes; `T_xX` the
classes over `x`.  For a chart `φ`, `TV = {[(x, φ, h)] | x ∈ V, h ∈ T_{φ(x)}O}` and
`Tφ : TV → TO`, `Tφ[(x, φ, h)] = (φ(x), h)`; the topology on `TX` is generated by the sets
`(Tφ)⁻¹(W)`, `W` open in `TO`.  (Proposition 2.3.15 (preprint 2.19)) (1) this is a Hausdorff topology; (2)
`p : TX → X¹` is continuous and open; (3) `TX` is metrizable, in particular paracompact.
The maps `Tφ` are homeomorphisms, `Tφ' ∘ (Tφ)⁻¹ = T(φ' ∘ φ⁻¹)` (formula (5)) is sc-smooth, and
`(TV, Tφ, (TO, TC, TE))` is an sc-smooth atlas: `TX` is an M-polyfold and `p : TX → X¹` is
sc-smooth.

## What is formalized

* The tangent of the local data: `Polyfold.ScOperator.isScSmooth` (sc-operators are sc-smooth),
  `IsPartialQuadrant.tangentSet` (`TC` is a partial quadrant in `TE`),
  `IsRelOpenInQuadrant.tangentSet`, `ScRetraction.tangentRetraction` (`Tr : TU → TU`, with
  `tangentRetraction_retract : Tr(TU) = TO`), `IsScRetract.tangentSet`, `LocalModel.tangent`
  (`(TO, TC, TE)`), and the **tangent functor** `IsScSmoothRetractMap.tangent`: `Tf` is sc-smooth
  `(TO, TC, TE) → (TO', TC', TE')`; `retractTangentMap_id` (`T(id) = id`), with Theorem 2.1.15 (preprint 2.8) the
  functoriality.
* The locality of the tangent construction, used throughout: `retractTangent_inter_isOpen`
  (`T(O ∩ W) = TO ∩ (W₁ ⊕ E)`) and `retractTangentMap_inter_isOpen` (`Tf` computed on the open
  subset `O ∩ W` is `Tf` computed on `O`), `retractTangentMap_congr`.
* `MPolyfold.TangentPre P`: the tuples `(x, φ, h)` (Definition 2.3.12 (preprint 2.17)), `TangentPre.Rel`
  (the equivalence, in the form `T(ψ ∘ φ⁻¹)(φ(x), h) = (ψ(x), h')`), the key identity
  `TangentPre.Rel.transport` (`T(χ ∘ φ⁻¹)(φ(x), h) = T(χ ∘ ψ⁻¹)(ψ(x), h')` for every third chart
  `χ`), `TangentPre.setoid`, and `MPolyfold.TangentSpace P = TX` (**Definition 2.3.14 (preprint 2.18)**),
  `MPolyfold.tangentProj : TX → X¹` and `MPolyfold.tangentFiber P x = T_xX`.
* `MPolyfold.tangentChartSet hφ = TV`, `MPolyfold.tangentChartMap hφ = Tφ` (with `chartMap_fst`,
  `chartMap_mem_retractTangent`, `tangentChartMap_injOn`), the topology
  `instTopologicalSpaceTangentSpace` (generated by the text's family), **Proposition 2.3.15 (preprint 2.19) (1)**
  (the instance `T2Space (P.TangentSpace)`), **Proposition 2.3.15 (preprint 2.19) (2)** in the form
  `continuous_tangentProj` (continuity; openness is not needed and not proved: gap G.8 of the
  report).
* `MPolyfold.tangentChart hφ α₀ : MChart P.TangentSpace`, the chart `(TV, Tφ, (TO, TC, TE))`;
  `tangentChart_overlap` (`Tφ(TV ∩ TV') = T(φ(V ∩ V'))`), `tangentChart_transition` (formula (5)),
  `tangentChart_compatible`, `MPolyfold.tangentPolyfold P : MPolyfold P.TangentSpace` (`TX` as an
  M-polyfold, with the instance argument `[ParacompactSpace P.TangentSpace]`, supplied by
  `MPolyfold.paracompactSpace_tangentSpace` in `Metrizable.lean`), and
  `MPolyfold.tangentProj_isScSmooth`:
  `p : TX → X¹` is sc-smooth.

## What the text leaves implicit, and the choices made

* The text never checks that the equivalence of Definition 2.3.12 (preprint 2.17) is an equivalence relation, nor
  that `Tφ` is well defined on classes; both need the chain rule (Theorem 2.1.15 (preprint 2.8)), `T(id) = id`, and
  the locality of `Tf` (the chain rule applies on the triple overlap `φ(V ∩ V' ∩ V'')`, an open
  subset of `φ(V ∩ V')`, and `Tf` computed there must agree with `Tf` computed on `φ(V ∩ V')`).
  This is `TangentPre.Rel.transport`.
* `TC` is a partial quadrant in `TE` through the sc-isomorphism `TE ≅ ℝⁿ ⊕ (W¹ ⊕ (ℝⁿ ⊕ W))`,
  `((a, w), (b, v)) ↦ (a, (w, (b, v)))`, which the text does not write down.
* Paracompactness of `TX` (Proposition 2.3.15 (preprint 2.19) (3)) is an instance argument
  `[ParacompactSpace P.TangentSpace]` of `tangentPolyfold`, because this file comes before the
  metrizability proof.  It is not an added hypothesis: `TX` is proved metrizable and paracompact
  in `Metrizable.lean` (`Polyfold.proposition_2_3_15_three`, the instance
  `MPolyfold.paracompactSpace_tangentSpace`), so wherever that file is imported the argument is
  filled in automatically.  The text's proof uses Smirnov's theorem, Proposition 2.7.4 (preprint 2.57) and the
  paracompactness of `X¹`; the formal proof pulls a partition of unity of `X` back along
  `TX → X¹ → X` (`Polyfold.metrizableSpace_of_pullback`) and avoids Proposition 2.7.4 (preprint 2.57) (G.15).
  Hausdorffness is proved as in the text.
* The chart inverse is a total function, so `tangentChart` carries a junk value `α₀ : TX`.
* `p : TX → X¹` sc-smooth is read through Definition 2.3.8 (preprint 2.14) with the charts `Tφ` of `TX` and the
  level charts `φ` of `X¹` (`MPolyfold.shift`); its coordinate representation is the projection
  `TO → O₁`, which is sc-smooth since `pr₁ ∘ Tr = r₁ ∘ pr₁` on `TU`.
-/

open Set Filter Topology Function

noncomputable section

namespace Polyfold

variable {E E' E'' : ScBanach}

/-! ### Sc-operators are sc-smooth -/

/-- An sc-operator is sc-smooth on every sc-domain (its level maps are continuous linear). -/
theorem ScOperator.isScSmooth {F : ScBanach} (T : ScOperator E F) {U : Set (E 0)}
    (hU : IsScDomain E U) : IsScSmooth U (T 0) := by
  refine IsScSmooth.of_contDiffOn_levels hU (fun m x _ => ⟨T m x, T.toBase_comm m x⟩) fun m => ?_
  have : levelMap (T 0) m = T m := funext fun x => T.levelMap_eq m x
  rw [this]
  exact (T m).contDiff.contDiffOn

/-- The projection `TE = E¹ ⊕ E → E¹` as an sc-operator. -/
def ScBanach.tangentFst (E : ScBanach) : ScOperator E.tangent E.shift where
  lvl m := ContinuousLinearMap.fst ℝ (E (m + 1)) (E m)
  incl_comm _ _ := rfl

/-! ### The tangent `(TO, TC, TE)` of a local model (Definition 2.1.12 (preprint 2.5)) -/

section TangentModel

variable {n : ℕ} {W : ScBanach}

/-- The re-association `((a, w), (b, v)) ↦ (a, (w, (b, v)))` of `T(ℝⁿ ⊕ W) = (ℝⁿ ⊕ W¹) ⊕ (ℝⁿ ⊕ W)`
onto `ℝⁿ ⊕ (W¹ ⊕ (ℝⁿ ⊕ W))`, as an sc-isomorphism. -/
def tangentQuadrantIso (n : ℕ) (W : ScBanach) :
    ScIso ((ScBanach.const (Fin n → ℝ)).prod W).tangent
      ((ScBanach.const (Fin n → ℝ)).prod (W.shift.prod ((ScBanach.const (Fin n → ℝ)).prod W))) where
  lvl m := ContinuousLinearEquiv.prodAssoc ℝ (Fin n → ℝ) (W (m + 1)) ((Fin n → ℝ) × W m)
  incl_comm _ _ := rfl

/-- The tangent `TC = C¹ ⊕ E` of a partial quadrant is a partial quadrant in `TE` (the remark
after Definition 2.1.12 (preprint 2.5)). -/
theorem IsPartialQuadrant.tangentSet {C : Set (E 0)} (hC : IsPartialQuadrant E C) :
    IsPartialQuadrant E.tangent (E.tangentSet C) := by
  obtain ⟨n, W, T, rfl⟩ := hC
  -- `T' = assoc ∘ (T¹ × T)`
  let T₁ : ScIso E.tangent ((ScBanach.const (Fin n → ℝ)).prod W).tangent :=
    { lvl := fun m => (T (m + 1)).prodCongr (T m)
      incl_comm := fun m x => Prod.ext (T.incl_comm (m + 1) x.1) (T.incl_comm m x.2) }
  refine ⟨n, W.shift.prod ((ScBanach.const (Fin n → ℝ)).prod W), T₁.trans (tangentQuadrantIso n W),
    ?_⟩
  ext p
  change p.1 ∈ E.lvlSet (T 0 ⁻¹' quadrant n W 0) 1 ↔ _
  rw [IsPartialQuadrant.lvlSet_eq T 1]
  rfl

/-- `TU = U¹ ⊕ E` is relatively open in `TC`. -/
theorem IsRelOpenInQuadrant.tangentSet {C U : Set (E 0)} (hU : IsRelOpenInQuadrant E C U) :
    IsRelOpenInQuadrant E.tangent (E.tangentSet C) (E.tangentSet U) := by
  obtain ⟨O, hO, rfl⟩ := hU.relOpen
  refine ⟨hU.isPartialQuadrant.tangentSet, E.lvlSet O 1 ×ˢ univ,
    (E.isOpen_lvlSet hO 1).prod isOpen_univ, ?_⟩
  ext p
  change p.1 ∈ E.lvlSet (O ∩ C) 1 ↔ (p.1 ∈ E.lvlSet O 1 ∧ p.2 ∈ univ) ∧ p.1 ∈ E.lvlSet C 1
  rw [ScBanach.lvlSet_inter]
  simp only [mem_inter_iff, mem_univ, and_true]

variable {C : Set (E 0)}

/-- The tangent `Tr : TU → TU` of an sc-smooth retraction is an sc-smooth retraction on `TU`
(the remark after Definition 2.1.16 (preprint 2.9)). -/
def ScRetraction.tangentRetraction (R : ScRetraction E C) : ScRetraction E.tangent (E.tangentSet C) where
  U := E.tangentSet R.U
  toFun := tangentMap R.U R
  relOpen := R.relOpen.tangentSet
  mapsTo := R.tangentMap_mapsTo
  isScSmooth := LocalModel.tangent_isScSmooth R
  idem _ hp := R.tangentMap_tangentMap hp

@[simp] lemma ScRetraction.tangentRetraction_U (R : ScRetraction E C) :
    R.tangentRetraction.U = E.tangentSet R.U := rfl

@[simp] lemma ScRetraction.tangentRetraction_apply (R : ScRetraction E C) (p : E.tangent 0) :
    R.tangentRetraction p = tangentMap R.U R p := rfl

/-- `Tr(TU) = TO`. -/
theorem ScRetraction.tangentRetraction_retract (R : ScRetraction E C) :
    R.tangentRetraction.retract = retractTangent E C R.retract := by
  rw [retractTangent_eq]; rfl

/-- `(TO, TC, TE)` is an sc-smooth retract (Definition 2.1.12 (preprint 2.5)). -/
theorem IsScRetract.tangentSet {O : Set (E 0)} (hO : IsScRetract E C O) :
    IsScRetract E.tangent (E.tangentSet C) (retractTangent E C O) := by
  obtain ⟨R, rfl⟩ := hO
  exact ⟨R.tangentRetraction, R.tangentRetraction_retract⟩

/-- The tangent `(TO, TC, TE)` of a local model (Definition 2.1.12 (preprint 2.5)). -/
def LocalModel.tangent (M : LocalModel) : LocalModel :=
  ⟨M.E.tangent, M.E.tangentSet M.C, retractTangent M.E M.C M.O, M.isScRetract.tangentSet⟩

@[simp] lemma LocalModel.tangent_E (M : LocalModel) : M.tangent.E = M.E.tangent := rfl
@[simp] lemma LocalModel.tangent_O (M : LocalModel) : M.tangent.O = retractTangent M.E M.C M.O := rfl
@[simp] lemma LocalModel.tangent_C (M : LocalModel) : M.tangent.C = M.E.tangentSet M.C := rfl

/-- `TO ⊆ TU` and the base points of `TO` lie in `O₁`. -/
lemma retractTangent_fst_mem {O : Set (E 0)} (hO : IsScRetract E C O) {p : E.tangent 0}
    (hp : p ∈ retractTangent E C O) : p.1 ∈ E.lvlSet O 1 := by
  obtain ⟨R, rfl⟩ := hO
  rw [retractTangent_eq] at hp
  exact R.fst_mem_of_mem_tangent hp

/-- `(x, 0) ∈ TO` for `x ∈ O₁`. -/
lemma mk_zero_mem_retractTangent {O : Set (E 0)} (hO : IsScRetract E C O) {x : E 1}
    (hx : x ∈ E.lvlSet O 1) : ((x, 0) : E.tangent 0) ∈ retractTangent E C O := by
  obtain ⟨R, rfl⟩ := hO
  rw [retractTangent_eq, R.mem_tangent_iff_of_mem hx, map_zero]

/-! ### Locality of the tangent construction -/

/-- **`T(O ∩ W) = TO ∩ (W₁ ⊕ E)`**: the tangent of an open subset of a retract. -/
theorem retractTangent_inter_isOpen {O : Set (E 0)} (hO : IsScRetract E C O) {W : Set (E 0)}
    (hW : IsOpen W) :
    retractTangent E C (O ∩ W) = retractTangent E C O ∩ (E.lvlSet W 1 ×ˢ univ) := by
  obtain ⟨R, rfl⟩ := hO
  rw [← R.restrict_retract hW, retractTangent_eq, retractTangent_eq]
  have hsub : (R.restrict hW).U ⊆ R.U := inter_subset_left
  have heq := R.isSc1.tangentMap_eqOn_of_subset (R.restrict hW).isScDomain hsub
  ext p
  rw [(R.restrict hW).mem_tangent_iff, mem_inter_iff, R.mem_tangent_iff]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨hp, hfix⟩
    have hpU : p ∈ E.tangentSet R.U := E.tangentSet_mono hsub hp
    refine ⟨⟨hpU, ?_⟩, ?_, mem_univ _⟩
    · have hfix' : tangentMap (R.restrict hW).U R p = p := hfix
      rw [← heq hp]; exact hfix'
    · have : p.1 ∈ E.lvlSet (R.U ∩ R ⁻¹' W) 1 := hp
      rw [ScBanach.lvlSet_inter] at this
      have h1 : R (E.toBase 1 p.1) ∈ W := this.2
      have h2 : levelMap R 1 p.1 = p.1 := congrArg Prod.fst hfix
      have h3 : E.toBase 1 (levelMap R 1 p.1) = R (E.toBase 1 p.1) :=
        R.isSc1.isSc0.toBase_levelMap this.1
      rw [h2] at h3
      change E.toBase 1 p.1 ∈ W
      rw [h3]; exact h1
  · rintro ⟨⟨hpU, hfix⟩, hpW, -⟩
    have h2 : levelMap R 1 p.1 = p.1 := congrArg Prod.fst hfix
    have h3 : E.toBase 1 (levelMap R 1 p.1) = R (E.toBase 1 p.1) :=
      R.isSc1.isSc0.toBase_levelMap hpU
    rw [h2] at h3
    have hp : p ∈ E.tangentSet (R.restrict hW).U := by
      change p.1 ∈ E.lvlSet (R.U ∩ R ⁻¹' W) 1
      rw [ScBanach.lvlSet_inter]
      refine ⟨hpU, ?_⟩
      change R (E.toBase 1 p.1) ∈ W
      rw [← h3]; exact hpW
    refine ⟨hp, ?_⟩
    change tangentMap (R.restrict hW).U R p = p
    rw [heq hp]; exact hfix

lemma retractTangent_mono_inter {O : Set (E 0)} (hO : IsScRetract E C O) {W : Set (E 0)}
    (hW : IsOpen W) : retractTangent E C (O ∩ W) ⊆ retractTangent E C O := by
  rw [retractTangent_inter_isOpen hO hW]; exact inter_subset_left

variable {C' : Set (E' 0)} {C'' : Set (E'' 0)}

/-- `Tf` depends only on the values of `f` on `O`. -/
theorem retractTangentMap_congr {O : Set (E 0)} {O' : Set (E' 0)} {f f' : E 0 → E' 0}
    (hf : IsScSmoothRetractMap E C O E' C' O' f) (hO : IsScRetract E C O) (hff' : EqOn f f' O) :
    EqOn (retractTangentMap E C O f) (retractTangentMap E C O f') (retractTangent E C O) := by
  obtain ⟨R, rfl⟩ := hO
  intro p hp
  rw [retractTangentMap_eqOn hf R rfl hp, retractTangentMap_eqOn (hf.congr hff') R rfl hp]
  have hpU : p ∈ E.tangentSet R.U := by rw [retractTangent_eq] at hp; exact R.tangent_subset hp
  exact (hf.comp_isScSmooth R rfl).isSc1.tangentMap_congr R.isScDomain
    (fun y hy => hff' (R.apply_mem_retract hy)) hpU

/-- **`T(id) = id`** on `TO` (for any map agreeing with the identity on `O`). -/
theorem retractTangentMap_id {O : Set (E 0)} (hO : IsScRetract E C O) {f : E 0 → E 0}
    (hf : EqOn f id O) : EqOn (retractTangentMap E C O f) id (retractTangent E C O) := by
  refine (retractTangentMap_congr ((isScSmoothRetractMap_id O).congr hf.symm) hO hf).trans ?_
  obtain ⟨R, rfl⟩ := hO
  intro p hp
  rw [retractTangentMap_eqOn (isScSmoothRetractMap_id _) R rfl hp]
  rw [retractTangent_eq] at hp
  exact (R.mem_tangent_iff.1 hp).2

/-- **Locality of `Tf`**: on the open subset `O ∩ W` of `O`, `Tf` computed for `(O ∩ W, C, E)`
agrees with `Tf` computed for `(O, C, E)`. -/
theorem retractTangentMap_inter_isOpen {O : Set (E 0)} {O' : Set (E' 0)} {f : E 0 → E' 0}
    (hf : IsScSmoothRetractMap E C O E' C' O' f) (hO : IsScRetract E C O) {W : Set (E 0)}
    (hW : IsOpen W) :
    EqOn (retractTangentMap E C (O ∩ W) f) (retractTangentMap E C O f)
      (retractTangent E C (O ∩ W)) := by
  obtain ⟨R, rfl⟩ := hO
  intro p hp
  have hp' : p ∈ retractTangent E C R.retract := retractTangent_mono_inter R.isScRetract hW hp
  rw [retractTangentMap_eqOn hf R rfl hp',
    retractTangentMap_eqOn (hf.restrict R.isScRetract) (R.restrict hW) (R.restrict_retract hW) hp]
  have hsub : (R.restrict hW).U ⊆ R.U := inter_subset_left
  have hpU : p ∈ E.tangentSet (R.restrict hW).U := by
    rw [← R.restrict_retract hW, retractTangent_eq] at hp
    exact (R.restrict hW).tangent_subset hp
  exact (hf.comp_isScSmooth R rfl).isSc1.tangentMap_eqOn_of_subset (R.restrict hW).isScDomain hsub hpU

/-! ### The tangent functor -/

/-- **The tangent functor** (the paragraph after Theorem 2.1.15 (preprint 2.8)): if `f : (O, C, E) → (O', C', E')` is
sc-smooth then `Tf : (TO, TC, TE) → (TO', TC', TE')` is sc-smooth. -/
theorem IsScSmoothRetractMap.tangent {O : Set (E 0)} {O' : Set (E' 0)} {f : E 0 → E' 0}
    (hf : IsScSmoothRetractMap E C O E' C' O' f) (hO : IsScRetract E C O) (hO' : IsScRetract E' C' O') :
    IsScSmoothRetractMap E.tangent (E.tangentSet C) (retractTangent E C O) E'.tangent
      (E'.tangentSet C') (retractTangent E' C' O') (retractTangentMap E C O f) := by
  rw [isScSmoothRetractMap_iff_exists hO.tangentSet]
  refine ⟨hf.tangentMap_mapsTo hO hO', ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨R, rfl⟩ := hO
  refine ⟨R.tangentRetraction, R.tangentRetraction_retract, ?_⟩
  have hsm : IsScSmooth (E.tangentSet R.U) (tangentMap R.U (f ∘ R)) :=
    (isScSmooth_iff.1 (hf.comp_isScSmooth R rfl)).2
  refine hsm.congr R.isScDomain.tangentSet fun p hp => ?_
  -- `T(f ∘ r)(p) = T(f ∘ r)(Tr p) = Tf(Tr p)` on `TU`
  have h1 : tangentMap R.U R p ∈ retractTangent E C R.retract := by
    rw [retractTangent_eq]; exact ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩
  change tangentMap R.U (f ∘ R) p = retractTangentMap E C R.retract f (tangentMap R.U R p)
  rw [retractTangentMap_eqOn hf R rfl h1]
  obtain ⟨_, hchain⟩ := theorem_1_3_1 R.relOpen R.relOpen R.isSc1 (hf.comp_isScSmooth R rfl).isSc1 R.mapsTo
  have hcongr : EqOn (tangentMap R.U (f ∘ R)) (tangentMap R.U ((f ∘ R) ∘ R)) (E.tangentSet R.U) :=
    (hf.comp_isScSmooth R rfl).isSc1.tangentMap_congr R.isScDomain fun y hy => by
      simp only [Function.comp_apply, R.idem y hy]
  exact ((hcongr hp).trans (hchain hp))

end TangentModel

/-! ### Transition maps on open subsets of overlaps -/

namespace MChart

variable {X : Type*} [TopologicalSpace X] (φ ψ : MChart X)

/-- The image `φ(s)` of an open `s ⊆ V ∩ V'` is an open subset of the overlap `φ(V ∩ V')`. -/
lemma image_eq_overlap_inter {s : Set X} (hs : s ⊆ φ.source ∩ ψ.source) (hso : IsOpen s) :
    ∃ W : Set (φ.model.E 0), IsOpen W ∧ φ '' s = φ.overlap ψ ∩ W := by
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hWeq⟩ := φ.exists_isOpen_image_eq (hs.trans inter_subset_left) hso
  refine ⟨W, hW, ?_⟩
  rw [hWeq]
  exact (inter_eq_inter_of_subset (φ.overlap_subset ψ) (hWeq ▸ image_mono hs)).symm

/-- The transition map `ψ ∘ φ⁻¹` of two compatible charts is sc-smooth `φ(s) → ψ(s)` for every open
`s ⊆ V ∩ V'`. -/
theorem Compatible.transition_image {φ ψ : MChart X} (h : φ.Compatible ψ) {s : Set X}
    (hs : s ⊆ φ.source ∩ ψ.source) (hso : IsOpen s) :
    IsScSmoothRetractMap φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ '' s) ψ.model.E ψ.model.C (ψ '' s)
      (φ.transition ψ) := by
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hWeq⟩ := φ.image_eq_overlap_inter ψ hs hso
  rw [hWeq]
  refine (h.1.restrict (φ.isScRetract_overlap ψ)).mono_target ?_
  rw [← hWeq]
  rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
  rw [φ.transition_apply ψ (hs hx).1]
  exact ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩

/-- `φ ∘ φ⁻¹ = id` on `O`. -/
lemma transition_self_eqOn : EqOn (φ.transition φ) id φ.model.O := fun z hz => by
  change φ (φ.symm z) = z
  exact φ.apply_symm_apply hz

end MChart

/-! ### The tangent bundle `TX` (Definitions 2.3.12, 2.3.14 (preprint 2.17, 2.18)) -/

namespace MPolyfold

universe u v

variable {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X] [T2Space X] [ParacompactSpace X] (P : MPolyfold X)

/-- The tuples `(x, V, φ, (O, C, E), h)` of Definition 2.3.12 (preprint 2.17): `x ∈ X₁`, `φ` a chart of the structure
around `x`, `h ∈ T_{φ(x)}O`. -/
structure TangentPre where
  /-- The point `x ∈ X₁`. -/
  x : X
  /-- The chart `φ` around `x`. -/
  φ : MChart X
  /-- The vector `h ∈ T_{φ(x)}O`. -/
  h : φ.model.E 0
  isChart : P.IsChart φ
  mem_source : x ∈ φ.source
  mem_level : x ∈ P.levelSet 1
  mem_tangent : ((levelLift φ 1 x, h) : φ.model.E.tangent 0) ∈
    retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C φ.model.O

namespace TangentPre

variable {P}

/-- The vector `(φ(x), h) ∈ TO ⊆ TE₀`. -/
def vec (p : P.TangentPre) : p.φ.model.E.tangent 0 := (levelLift p.φ 1 p.x, p.h)

lemma vec_mem (p : P.TangentPre) :
    p.vec ∈ retractTangent p.φ.model.E p.φ.model.C p.φ.model.O := p.mem_tangent

lemma toBase_vec_fst (p : P.TangentPre) : p.φ.model.E.toBase 1 p.vec.1 = p.φ p.x :=
  P.toBase_levelLift p.isChart p.mem_source p.mem_level

omit [T2Space X] [ParacompactSpace X] in
/-- For `a ∈ TO` with base point in the open subset `φ(s)`, `a ∈ T(φ(s))`. -/
lemma mem_retractTangent_image_iff {φ : MChart X} {s : Set X} (hs : s ⊆ φ.source) (hso : IsOpen s)
    {a : φ.model.E.tangent 0} (ha : φ.model.E.toBase 1 a.1 ∈ φ '' s) :
    a ∈ retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ '' s) ↔
      a ∈ retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C φ.model.O := by
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hWeq⟩ := φ.exists_isOpen_image_eq hs hso
  rw [hWeq, retractTangent_inter_isOpen φ.model.isScRetract hW]
  have : a.1 ∈ φ.model.E.lvlSet W 1 := by
    change φ.model.E.toBase 1 a.1 ∈ W
    rw [hWeq] at ha; exact ha.2
  exact ⟨fun h => h.1, fun h => ⟨h, this, mem_univ _⟩⟩

lemma vec_mem_image (p : P.TangentPre) {s : Set X} (hs : s ⊆ p.φ.source) (hso : IsOpen s)
    (hx : p.x ∈ s) : p.vec ∈ retractTangent p.φ.model.E p.φ.model.C (p.φ '' s) :=
  (mem_retractTangent_image_iff hs hso (by rw [p.toBase_vec_fst]; exact ⟨p.x, hx, rfl⟩)).2 p.vec_mem

/-- The vector `(x, φ, h)` seen in another chart `ψ` around `x`: `T(ψ ∘ φ⁻¹)(φ(x), h)`. -/
def transport (p : P.TangentPre) (ψ : MChart X) : ψ.model.E.tangent 0 :=
  retractTangentMap p.φ.model.E p.φ.model.C (p.φ.overlap ψ) (p.φ.transition ψ) p.vec

/-- `T(φ ∘ φ⁻¹) = id`: transport to the own chart does nothing. -/
theorem transport_self (p : P.TangentPre) : p.transport p.φ = p.vec := by
  have hmem : p.vec ∈ retractTangent p.φ.model.E p.φ.model.C (p.φ.overlap p.φ) :=
    p.vec_mem_image inter_subset_left (p.φ.isOpen_source.inter p.φ.isOpen_source)
      ⟨p.mem_source, p.mem_source⟩
  exact retractTangentMap_id (p.φ.isScRetract_overlap p.φ)
    ((p.φ.transition_self_eqOn).mono (p.φ.overlap_subset p.φ)) hmem

/-- The transported vector lies in `TO'`. -/
theorem transport_mem (p : P.TangentPre) {ψ : MChart X} (hψ : P.IsChart ψ) (hx : p.x ∈ ψ.source) :
    p.transport ψ ∈ retractTangent ψ.model.E ψ.model.C ψ.model.O := by
  have h := (p.isChart.compatible hψ (P := P)).1.tangentMap_mapsTo (p.φ.isScRetract_overlap ψ)
    (ψ.isScRetract_overlap p.φ)
    (p.vec_mem_image inter_subset_left (p.φ.isOpen_source.inter ψ.isOpen_source)
      ⟨p.mem_source, hx⟩)
  exact (mem_retractTangent_image_iff inter_subset_left (ψ.isOpen_source.inter p.φ.isOpen_source)
    (retractTangent_fst_mem (ψ.isScRetract_overlap p.φ) h)).1 h

/-- The base point of the transported vector is `ψ(x)`. -/
theorem transport_fst (p : P.TangentPre) {ψ : MChart X} (hψ : P.IsChart ψ) (hx : p.x ∈ ψ.source) :
    (p.transport ψ).1 = levelLift ψ 1 p.x := by
  have hcomp := (p.isChart.compatible hψ (P := P)).1
  obtain ⟨R, hR⟩ := p.φ.isScRetract_overlap ψ
  have hmem : p.vec ∈ retractTangent p.φ.model.E p.φ.model.C (p.φ.overlap ψ) :=
    p.vec_mem_image inter_subset_left (p.φ.isOpen_source.inter ψ.isOpen_source) ⟨p.mem_source, hx⟩
  rw [transport, retractTangentMap_apply hcomp R hR hmem]
  apply ψ.model.E.toBase_injective 1
  have hsc : IsSc0 p.φ.model.E ψ.model.E R.U (p.φ.transition ψ ∘ R) :=
    (hcomp.comp_isScSmooth R hR).isSc1.isSc0
  have h1 : p.vec.1 ∈ p.φ.model.E.lvlSet R.U 1 := by
    apply R.lvlSet_retract_subset 1
    rw [hR]
    exact retractTangent_fst_mem (p.φ.isScRetract_overlap ψ) hmem
  have h2 : p.φ p.x ∈ R.retract := by rw [hR]; exact p.φ.mem_overlap ψ p.mem_source hx
  rw [hsc.toBase_levelMap h1, Function.comp_apply, p.toBase_vec_fst,
    R.apply_eq_self_of_mem_retract h2, p.φ.transition_apply ψ p.mem_source,
    P.toBase_levelLift hψ hx p.mem_level]

/-- **The chain rule for transports**: transporting `(x, φ, h)` to `ψ` and then to `χ` is
transporting it to `χ`.  (The chain rule, Theorem 2.1.15 (preprint 2.8), on the triple overlap, together with the
locality of `Tf`.) -/
theorem transport_transport (p : P.TangentPre) {ψ χ : MChart X} (hψ : P.IsChart ψ)
    (hχ : P.IsChart χ) (hxψ : p.x ∈ ψ.source) (hxχ : p.x ∈ χ.source) :
    retractTangentMap ψ.model.E ψ.model.C (ψ.overlap χ) (ψ.transition χ) (p.transport ψ) =
      p.transport χ := by
  set φ := p.φ with hφdef
  have hφ : P.IsChart φ := p.isChart
  -- the triple overlap
  set s := φ.source ∩ ψ.source ∩ χ.source with hs
  have hso : IsOpen s := (φ.isOpen_source.inter ψ.isOpen_source).inter χ.isOpen_source
  have hxs : p.x ∈ s := ⟨⟨p.mem_source, hxψ⟩, hxχ⟩
  have hsφψ : s ⊆ φ.source ∩ ψ.source := fun y hy => hy.1
  have hsψχ : s ⊆ ψ.source ∩ χ.source := fun y hy => ⟨hy.1.2, hy.2⟩
  have hsφχ : s ⊆ φ.source ∩ χ.source := fun y hy => ⟨hy.1.1, hy.2⟩
  have hf := (hφ.compatible hψ (P := P)).transition_image hsφψ hso
  have hg := (hψ.compatible hχ (P := P)).transition_image hsψχ hso
  have hφs : IsScRetract φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ '' s) := φ.isScRetract_image (fun y hy => hy.1.1) hso
  have hψs : IsScRetract ψ.model.E ψ.model.C (ψ '' s) := ψ.isScRetract_image (fun y hy => hy.1.2) hso
  have hvec : p.vec ∈ retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ '' s) :=
    p.vec_mem_image (fun y hy => hy.1.1) hso hxs
  -- the chain rule on `φ(s)`
  have hchain := retractTangentMap_comp hg hf hφs hψs hvec
  -- `χ ∘ φ⁻¹ = (χ ∘ ψ⁻¹) ∘ (ψ ∘ φ⁻¹)` on `φ(s)`
  have hcongr := retractTangentMap_congr (hg.comp hf hψs) hφs
    (f' := φ.transition χ) (fun z hz => by
      obtain ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩ := hz
      exact (φ.transition_eq_comp_on χ ψ hy.1.1 hy.1.2).symm) hvec
  -- locality: the three tangent maps on `s` are those on the overlaps
  obtain ⟨W₁, hW₁, hW₁eq⟩ := φ.image_eq_overlap_inter χ hsφχ hso
  obtain ⟨W₂, hW₂, hW₂eq⟩ := φ.image_eq_overlap_inter ψ hsφψ hso
  obtain ⟨W₃, hW₃, hW₃eq⟩ := ψ.image_eq_overlap_inter χ hsψχ hso
  have hloc1 : retractTangentMap φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ '' s) (φ.transition χ) p.vec =
      p.transport χ := by
    change _ = retractTangentMap φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ.overlap χ) (φ.transition χ) p.vec
    have := retractTangentMap_inter_isOpen (hφ.compatible hχ (P := P)).1
      (φ.isScRetract_overlap χ) hW₁ (hW₁eq ▸ hvec)
    rw [← hW₁eq] at this
    exact this
  have hloc2 : retractTangentMap φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ '' s) (φ.transition ψ) p.vec =
      p.transport ψ := by
    change _ = retractTangentMap φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ.overlap ψ) (φ.transition ψ) p.vec
    have := retractTangentMap_inter_isOpen (hφ.compatible hψ (P := P)).1
      (φ.isScRetract_overlap ψ) hW₂ (hW₂eq ▸ hvec)
    rw [← hW₂eq] at this
    exact this
  have hTf : retractTangentMap φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ '' s) (φ.transition ψ) p.vec ∈
      retractTangent ψ.model.E ψ.model.C (ψ '' s) := hf.tangentMap_mapsTo hφs hψs hvec
  have hloc3 : retractTangentMap ψ.model.E ψ.model.C (ψ '' s) (ψ.transition χ)
      (retractTangentMap φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ '' s) (φ.transition ψ) p.vec) =
      retractTangentMap ψ.model.E ψ.model.C (ψ.overlap χ) (ψ.transition χ)
        (retractTangentMap φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ '' s) (φ.transition ψ) p.vec) := by
    have := retractTangentMap_inter_isOpen (hψ.compatible hχ (P := P)).1
      (ψ.isScRetract_overlap χ) hW₃ (hW₃eq ▸ hTf)
    rw [← hW₃eq] at this
    exact this
  rw [← hloc2, ← hloc3, ← hloc1, ← hcongr, hchain]
  rfl

/-- **Definition 2.3.12 (preprint 2.17)**: the tuples `(x, φ, h)` and `(x', ψ, h')` are **equivalent** if `x = x'`
and `T(ψ ∘ φ⁻¹)(φ(x), h) = (ψ(x), h')`. -/
def Rel (p q : P.TangentPre) : Prop := p.x = q.x ∧ p.transport q.φ = q.vec

theorem Rel.refl (p : P.TangentPre) : Rel p p := ⟨rfl, p.transport_self⟩

/-- Equivalent tuples transport to the same vector in every chart. -/
theorem Rel.transport {p q : P.TangentPre} (h : Rel p q) {χ : MChart X} (hχ : P.IsChart χ)
    (hx : p.x ∈ χ.source) : p.transport χ = q.transport χ := by
  rw [← p.transport_transport q.isChart hχ (h.1 ▸ q.mem_source) hx, h.2]
  rfl

theorem Rel.symm {p q : P.TangentPre} (h : Rel p q) : Rel q p := by
  refine ⟨h.1.symm, ?_⟩
  change retractTangentMap _ _ (q.φ.overlap p.φ) (q.φ.transition p.φ) q.vec = p.vec
  rw [← h.2, p.transport_transport q.isChart p.isChart (h.1 ▸ q.mem_source) p.mem_source,
    p.transport_self]

theorem Rel.trans {p q r : P.TangentPre} (h₁ : Rel p q) (h₂ : Rel q r) : Rel p r :=
  ⟨h₁.1.trans h₂.1, by rw [h₁.transport r.isChart (h₁.1 ▸ h₂.1 ▸ r.mem_source), h₂.2]⟩

/-- The equivalence relation of Definition 2.3.12 (preprint 2.17). -/
def setoid (P : MPolyfold X) : Setoid P.TangentPre where
  r := Rel
  iseqv := ⟨Rel.refl, Rel.symm, Rel.trans⟩

end TangentPre

/-- **Definition 2.3.14 (preprint 2.18)**: the **tangent bundle** `TX`, the set of equivalence classes of tuples
`(x, φ, h)`. -/
def TangentSpace : Type (max u 1) := Quotient (TangentPre.setoid P)

namespace TangentSpace

variable {P}

/-- The class of a tuple. -/
def mk (p : P.TangentPre) : P.TangentSpace := Quotient.mk (TangentPre.setoid P) p

lemma mk_eq_mk {p q : P.TangentPre} : mk p = mk q ↔ TangentPre.Rel p q := Quotient.eq

lemma sound {p q : P.TangentPre} (h : TangentPre.Rel p q) : mk p = mk q := Quotient.sound h

lemma ind {motive : P.TangentSpace → Prop} (h : ∀ p, motive (mk p)) (α : P.TangentSpace) :
    motive α := Quotient.ind h α

lemma exists_rep (α : P.TangentSpace) : ∃ p, mk p = α := Quotient.exists_rep α

/-- Lifting a function on tuples which respects the equivalence. -/
def lift {β : Sort*} (f : P.TangentPre → β) (h : ∀ p q, TangentPre.Rel p q → f p = f q) :
    P.TangentSpace → β := Quotient.lift f h

@[simp] lemma lift_mk {β : Sort*} (f : P.TangentPre → β) (h) (p : P.TangentPre) :
    lift f h (mk p) = f p := rfl

end TangentSpace

/-! ### The projection `p : TX → X¹` and the fibres `T_xX` -/

/-- The projection `p : TX → X¹`, `[(x, φ, h)] ↦ x`. -/
def tangentProj : P.TangentSpace → P.Level 1 :=
  TangentSpace.lift (fun p => P.levelMk 1 p.x p.mem_level) fun _ _ h => level_ext h.1

@[simp] lemma tangentProj_mk (p : P.TangentPre) :
    P.levelVal 1 (P.tangentProj (TangentSpace.mk p)) = p.x := rfl

/-- The **tangent space** `T_xX` at `x ∈ X₁` (Definition 2.3.14 (preprint 2.18)): the classes over `x`. -/
def tangentFiber (x : P.Level 1) : Set P.TangentSpace := {α | P.tangentProj α = x}

/-! ### The sets `TV` and the maps `Tφ` -/

section Chart

open scoped Classical

variable {P} {φ ψ χ : MChart X}

variable (φ) in
/-- `TV = p⁻¹(V₁)`, the part of `TX` over the domain of the chart `φ`. -/
def tangentChartSet : Set P.TangentSpace := {α | P.levelVal 1 (P.tangentProj α) ∈ φ.source}

lemma mk_mem_tangentChartSet {p : P.TangentPre} :
    TangentSpace.mk p ∈ tangentChartSet (P := P) φ ↔ p.x ∈ φ.source := Iff.rfl

open scoped Classical in
/-- `Tφ : TX → TO ⊆ TE₀`, `[(x, ψ, h)] ↦ T(φ ∘ ψ⁻¹)(ψ(x), h)` on `TV` (junk `0` off `TV`). -/
def tangentChartMap (hφ : P.IsChart φ) : P.TangentSpace → φ.model.E.tangent 0 :=
  TangentSpace.lift (fun p => if p.x ∈ φ.source then p.transport φ else 0) fun p q h => by
    by_cases hx : p.x ∈ φ.source
    · rw [if_pos hx, if_pos (h.1 ▸ hx), h.transport hφ hx]
    · rw [if_neg hx, if_neg (h.1 ▸ hx)]

variable (hφ : P.IsChart φ)

lemma tangentChartMap_mk {p : P.TangentPre} (hx : p.x ∈ φ.source) :
    tangentChartMap hφ (TangentSpace.mk p) = p.transport φ := by
  change (if p.x ∈ φ.source then p.transport φ else 0) = _
  rw [if_pos hx]

/-- `Tφ[(x, φ, h)] = (φ(x), h)`. -/
lemma tangentChartMap_mk_self (p : P.TangentPre) :
    tangentChartMap p.isChart (TangentSpace.mk p) = p.vec := by
  rw [tangentChartMap_mk p.isChart p.mem_source, p.transport_self]

lemma tangentChartMap_mem {α : P.TangentSpace} (hα : α ∈ tangentChartSet φ) :
    tangentChartMap hφ α ∈ retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C φ.model.O := by
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := TangentSpace.exists_rep α
  rw [tangentChartMap_mk hφ hα]
  exact p.transport_mem hφ hα

lemma tangentChartMap_fst {α : P.TangentSpace} (hα : α ∈ tangentChartSet φ) :
    (tangentChartMap hφ α).1 = levelLift φ 1 (P.levelVal 1 (P.tangentProj α)) := by
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := TangentSpace.exists_rep α
  rw [tangentChartMap_mk hφ hα, p.transport_fst hφ hα]
  rfl

/-- `Tφ` is injective on `TV`. -/
theorem tangentChartMap_injOn : InjOn (tangentChartMap hφ) (tangentChartSet φ) := by
  intro α hα β hβ heq
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := TangentSpace.exists_rep α
  obtain ⟨q, rfl⟩ := TangentSpace.exists_rep β
  have hx : p.x = q.x := by
    have h1 := congrArg Prod.fst heq
    rw [tangentChartMap_fst hφ hα, tangentChartMap_fst hφ hβ] at h1
    have h2 := congrArg (φ.model.E.toBase 1) h1
    rw [P.toBase_levelLift hφ hα p.mem_level, P.toBase_levelLift hφ hβ q.mem_level] at h2
    exact φ.toPartialEquiv.injOn hα hβ h2
  refine TangentSpace.sound ⟨hx, ?_⟩
  rw [tangentChartMap_mk hφ hα, tangentChartMap_mk hφ hβ] at heq
  rw [← p.transport_transport hφ q.isChart hα (hx ▸ q.mem_source), heq,
    q.transport_transport hφ q.isChart hβ q.mem_source, q.transport_self]

/-- The tuple `(φ⁻¹(a), φ, h)` of a vector `a = (a, h) ∈ TO`: the inverse of `Tφ`. -/
def TangentPre.ofVec {a : φ.model.E.tangent 0}
    (ha : a ∈ retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C φ.model.O) : P.TangentPre where
  x := φ.symm (φ.model.E.toBase 1 a.1)
  φ := φ
  h := a.2
  isChart := hφ
  mem_source := φ.symm_mapsTo (retractTangent_fst_mem φ.model.isScRetract ha)
  mem_level := (P.mem_levelSet_iff hφ (φ.symm_mapsTo (retractTangent_fst_mem φ.model.isScRetract
    ha))).2 (by rw [φ.apply_symm_apply (retractTangent_fst_mem φ.model.isScRetract ha)]; exact ⟨_, rfl⟩)
  mem_tangent := by
    have hO : φ.model.E.toBase 1 a.1 ∈ φ.model.O := retractTangent_fst_mem φ.model.isScRetract ha
    have hlift : levelLift φ 1 (φ.symm (φ.model.E.toBase 1 a.1)) = a.1 := by
      apply φ.model.E.toBase_injective 1
      rw [P.toBase_levelLift hφ (φ.symm_mapsTo hO) ((P.mem_levelSet_iff hφ (φ.symm_mapsTo hO)).2
        (by rw [φ.apply_symm_apply hO]; exact ⟨_, rfl⟩)), φ.apply_symm_apply hO]
    rw [hlift]
    exact ha

lemma TangentPre.ofVec_x {a : φ.model.E.tangent 0}
    (ha : a ∈ retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C φ.model.O) :
    (TangentPre.ofVec hφ ha).x = φ.symm (φ.model.E.toBase 1 a.1) := rfl

lemma TangentPre.ofVec_vec {a : φ.model.E.tangent 0}
    (ha : a ∈ retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C φ.model.O) : (TangentPre.ofVec hφ ha).vec = a := by
  have hO : φ.model.E.toBase 1 a.1 ∈ φ.model.O := retractTangent_fst_mem φ.model.isScRetract ha
  have hlift : levelLift φ 1 (φ.symm (φ.model.E.toBase 1 a.1)) = a.1 := by
    apply φ.model.E.toBase_injective 1
    rw [P.toBase_levelLift hφ (φ.symm_mapsTo hO) (TangentPre.ofVec hφ ha).mem_level,
      φ.apply_symm_apply hO]
  exact Prod.ext hlift rfl

/-- `Tφ ∘ (Tφ)⁻¹ = id` on `TO`. -/
lemma tangentChartMap_mk_ofVec {a : φ.model.E.tangent 0}
    (ha : a ∈ retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C φ.model.O) :
    tangentChartMap hφ (TangentSpace.mk (TangentPre.ofVec hφ ha)) = a :=
  (tangentChartMap_mk_self (TangentPre.ofVec hφ ha)).trans (TangentPre.ofVec_vec hφ ha)

/-- `(Tφ)⁻¹ ∘ Tφ = id` on `TV`. -/
lemma mk_ofVec_tangentChartMap {α : P.TangentSpace} (hα : α ∈ tangentChartSet φ) :
    TangentSpace.mk (TangentPre.ofVec hφ (tangentChartMap_mem hφ hα)) = α := by
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := TangentSpace.exists_rep α
  refine (TangentSpace.sound ⟨?_, ?_⟩).symm
  · rw [TangentPre.ofVec_x, tangentChartMap_fst hφ hα, P.toBase_levelLift hφ hα p.mem_level,
      φ.symm_apply_apply hα]
    rfl
  · change p.transport φ = _
    rw [TangentPre.ofVec_vec, tangentChartMap_mk hφ hα]

/-- The transition map `Tψ ∘ (Tφ)⁻¹ = T(ψ ∘ φ⁻¹)` (formula (5)), on `T(φ(V ∩ V'))`. -/
lemma tangentChartMap_mk_ofVec_of_mem (hψ : P.IsChart ψ) {a : φ.model.E.tangent 0}
    (ha' : a ∈ retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C φ.model.O)
    (ha : a ∈ retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ.overlap ψ)) :
    tangentChartMap hψ (TangentSpace.mk (TangentPre.ofVec hφ ha')) =
      retractTangentMap φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ.overlap ψ) (φ.transition ψ) a := by
  have hov : φ.model.E.toBase 1 a.1 ∈ φ.overlap ψ :=
    retractTangent_fst_mem (φ.isScRetract_overlap ψ) ha
  have hx : (TangentPre.ofVec hφ ha').x ∈ ψ.source := by
    rw [TangentPre.ofVec_x]
    obtain ⟨y, hy, hyeq⟩ := hov
    rw [← hyeq, φ.symm_apply_apply hy.1]; exact hy.2
  rw [tangentChartMap_mk hψ hx]
  change retractTangentMap φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ.overlap ψ) (φ.transition ψ)
    (TangentPre.ofVec hφ ha').vec = _
  rw [TangentPre.ofVec_vec]

/-- `[(φ⁻¹(a), φ, h)] ∈ TV'` iff the base point `a` lies in `φ(V ∩ V')`. -/
lemma mk_ofVec_mem_tangentChartSet_iff {a : φ.model.E.tangent 0}
    (ha : a ∈ retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C φ.model.O) :
    TangentSpace.mk (TangentPre.ofVec hφ ha) ∈ tangentChartSet ψ ↔
      φ.model.E.toBase 1 a.1 ∈ φ.overlap ψ := by
  have hO : φ.model.E.toBase 1 a.1 ∈ φ.model.O := retractTangent_fst_mem φ.model.isScRetract ha
  rw [mk_mem_tangentChartSet, TangentPre.ofVec_x]
  constructor
  · intro h
    exact ⟨_, ⟨φ.symm_mapsTo hO, h⟩, φ.apply_symm_apply hO⟩
  · rintro ⟨y, hy, hyeq⟩
    rw [← hyeq, φ.symm_apply_apply hy.1]; exact hy.2

end Chart

/-! ### The topology on `TX` (Proposition 2.3.15 (preprint 2.19)) -/

section Topology

/-- The text's family `B`: the sets `(Tφ)⁻¹(W)`, `W` open in `TO` (here `{α ∈ TV | Tφ(α) ∈ W}`
with `W` open in `TE₀`, the same sets). -/
def tangentBasis : Set (Set P.TangentSpace) :=
  {s | ∃ (φ : MChart X) (hφ : P.IsChart φ) (W : Set (φ.model.E.tangent 0)), IsOpen W ∧
    s = {α | α ∈ tangentChartSet φ ∧ tangentChartMap hφ α ∈ W}}

/-- The topology on `TX` generated by `B`. -/
instance : TopologicalSpace P.TangentSpace := TopologicalSpace.generateFrom P.tangentBasis

variable {P} {φ : MChart X}

lemma isOpen_tangent_basic (hφ : P.IsChart φ) {W : Set (φ.model.E.tangent 0)} (hW : IsOpen W) :
    IsOpen {α : P.TangentSpace | α ∈ tangentChartSet φ ∧ tangentChartMap hφ α ∈ W} :=
  TopologicalSpace.isOpen_generateFrom_of_mem ⟨φ, hφ, W, hW, rfl⟩

/-- `TV` is open in `TX`. -/
lemma isOpen_tangentChartSet (hφ : P.IsChart φ) : IsOpen (tangentChartSet (P := P) φ) := by
  have := isOpen_tangent_basic hφ (W := univ) isOpen_univ
  simpa using this

/-- **Proposition 2.3.15 (preprint 2.19) (2)**, continuity: the projection `p : TX → X¹` is continuous. -/
theorem continuous_tangentProj : Continuous P.tangentProj := by
  refine continuous_generateFrom_iff.2 ?_
  rintro _ ⟨ψ, hψ, W, hW, rfl⟩
  convert isOpen_tangent_basic hψ (hW.prod isOpen_univ) using 1
  ext α
  change (P.levelVal 1 (P.tangentProj α) ∈ ψ.source ∧
    levelLift ψ 1 (P.levelVal 1 (P.tangentProj α)) ∈ W) ↔
    α ∈ tangentChartSet ψ ∧ tangentChartMap hψ α ∈ W ×ˢ univ
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨h1, h2⟩
    refine ⟨h1, ?_, mem_univ _⟩
    rw [tangentChartMap_fst hψ h1]; exact h2
  · rintro ⟨h1, h2, -⟩
    refine ⟨h1, ?_⟩
    rw [tangentChartMap_fst hψ h1] at h2; exact h2

/-- The base point map `TX → X` is continuous. -/
theorem continuous_levelVal_tangentProj : Continuous fun α : P.TangentSpace =>
    P.levelVal 1 (P.tangentProj α) :=
  (continuous_levelVal 1).comp continuous_tangentProj

/-- **Proposition 2.3.15 (preprint 2.19) (1)**: `TX` is Hausdorff. -/
instance : T2Space P.TangentSpace := by
  refine ⟨fun α β hne => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := TangentSpace.exists_rep α
  obtain ⟨q, rfl⟩ := TangentSpace.exists_rep β
  by_cases hx : p.x = q.x
  · -- the same base point: separate `Tφ(α) ≠ Tφ(β)` in `TE₀`
    have hq : q.x ∈ p.φ.source := hx ▸ p.mem_source
    have hne' : tangentChartMap p.isChart (TangentSpace.mk p) ≠
        tangentChartMap p.isChart (TangentSpace.mk q) :=
      fun h => hne (tangentChartMap_injOn p.isChart p.mem_source hq h)
    obtain ⟨u, v, hu, hv, hαu, hβv, huv⟩ := t2_separation hne'
    refine ⟨{α | α ∈ tangentChartSet p.φ ∧ tangentChartMap p.isChart α ∈ u},
      {α | α ∈ tangentChartSet p.φ ∧ tangentChartMap p.isChart α ∈ v},
      isOpen_tangent_basic p.isChart hu, isOpen_tangent_basic p.isChart hv,
      ⟨p.mem_source, hαu⟩, ⟨hq, hβv⟩, ?_⟩
    exact Set.disjoint_left.2 fun γ h1 h2 => Set.disjoint_left.1 huv h1.2 h2.2
  · -- different base points: separate them in `X`
    obtain ⟨A, B, hA, hB, hpA, hqB, hAB⟩ := t2_separation hx
    refine ⟨(fun α => P.levelVal 1 (P.tangentProj α)) ⁻¹' A,
      (fun α => P.levelVal 1 (P.tangentProj α)) ⁻¹' B,
      hA.preimage continuous_levelVal_tangentProj, hB.preimage continuous_levelVal_tangentProj,
      hpA, hqB, ?_⟩
    exact Set.disjoint_left.2 fun γ h1 h2 => Set.disjoint_left.1 hAB h1 h2

end Topology

/-! ### The charts `(TV, Tφ, (TO, TC, TE))` and `TX` as an M-polyfold -/

section TangentChart

open scoped Classical

variable {P} {φ ψ : MChart X} (hφ : P.IsChart φ) (α₀ : P.TangentSpace)

/-- The inverse `(Tφ)⁻¹ : TO → TV`, `a ↦ [(φ⁻¹(a), φ, h)]`, with the junk value `α₀` off `TO`. -/
def tangentChartInv (a : φ.model.E.tangent 0) : P.TangentSpace :=
  if h : a ∈ retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C φ.model.O then TangentSpace.mk (TangentPre.ofVec hφ h)
  else α₀

lemma tangentChartInv_of_mem {a : φ.model.E.tangent 0}
    (ha : a ∈ retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C φ.model.O) :
    tangentChartInv hφ α₀ a = TangentSpace.mk (TangentPre.ofVec hφ ha) := dif_pos ha

/-- **The chart `(TV, Tφ, (TO, TC, TE))` of `TX`** induced by the chart `φ` of `X`. -/
def tangentChart : MChart P.TangentSpace where
  model := φ.model.tangent
  toPartialEquiv :=
    { toFun := tangentChartMap hφ
      invFun := tangentChartInv hφ α₀
      source := tangentChartSet φ
      target := retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C φ.model.O
      map_source' := fun _ hα => tangentChartMap_mem hφ hα
      map_target' := fun a ha => by
        rw [tangentChartInv_of_mem hφ α₀ ha]
        exact (TangentPre.ofVec hφ ha).mem_source
      left_inv' := fun α hα => by
        rw [tangentChartInv_of_mem hφ α₀ (tangentChartMap_mem hφ hα)]
        exact mk_ofVec_tangentChartMap hφ hα
      right_inv' := fun a ha => by
        rw [tangentChartInv_of_mem hφ α₀ ha]
        exact tangentChartMap_mk_ofVec hφ ha }
  isOpen_source := isOpen_tangentChartSet hφ
  target_eq := rfl
  continuousOn_toFun := by
    rw [continuousOn_iff']
    intro W hW
    refine ⟨{α | α ∈ tangentChartSet φ ∧ tangentChartMap hφ α ∈ W}, isOpen_tangent_basic hφ hW, ?_⟩
    ext α
    exact ⟨fun h => ⟨⟨h.2, h.1⟩, h.2⟩, fun h => ⟨h.1.2, h.2⟩⟩
  continuousOn_invFun := by
    rw [continuousOn_iff_continuous_domRestrict]
    refine continuous_generateFrom_iff.2 ?_
    rintro _ ⟨ψ, hψ, W, hW, rfl⟩
    -- the preimage is `{a ∈ TO | a ∈ T(φ(V ∩ V')) ∧ T(ψ ∘ φ⁻¹)(a) ∈ W}`
    obtain ⟨W₀, hW₀, hW₀eq⟩ := φ.exists_isOpen_image_eq (s := φ.source ∩ ψ.source) inter_subset_left
      (φ.isOpen_source.inter ψ.isOpen_source)
    have hov : φ.overlap ψ = φ.model.O ∩ W₀ := hW₀eq
    have hTov : retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ.overlap ψ) =
        retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C φ.model.O ∩ (φ.model.E.lvlSet W₀ 1 ×ˢ univ) := by
      rw [hov, retractTangent_inter_isOpen φ.model.isScRetract hW₀]
    have hcont : ContinuousOn (retractTangentMap φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ.overlap ψ) (φ.transition ψ))
        (retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ.overlap ψ)) :=
      ((hφ.compatible hψ (P := P)).1.tangent (φ.isScRetract_overlap ψ)
        (ψ.isScRetract_overlap φ)).continuousOn (φ.isScRetract_overlap ψ).tangentSet
    obtain ⟨u, hu, hueq⟩ := (continuousOn_iff'.1 hcont) W hW
    refine isOpen_induced_iff.2 ⟨(φ.model.E.lvlSet W₀ 1 ×ˢ univ) ∩ u,
      ((φ.model.E.isOpen_lvlSet hW₀ 1).prod isOpen_univ).inter hu, ?_⟩
    ext ⟨a, ha⟩
    rw [iff_comm]
    have haO : a ∈ retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C φ.model.O := ha
    change (tangentChartInv hφ α₀ a ∈ tangentChartSet ψ ∧
      tangentChartMap hψ (tangentChartInv hφ α₀ a) ∈ W) ↔ _
    rw [tangentChartInv_of_mem hφ α₀ haO, mk_ofVec_mem_tangentChartSet_iff hφ haO]
    have hiff : φ.model.E.toBase 1 a.1 ∈ φ.overlap ψ ↔
        a ∈ retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ.overlap ψ) := by
      rw [hTov]
      constructor
      · intro h
        refine ⟨haO, ?_, mem_univ _⟩
        rw [hov] at h; exact h.2
      · rintro ⟨-, h, -⟩
        rw [hov]; exact ⟨retractTangent_fst_mem φ.model.isScRetract haO, h⟩
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨h1, h2⟩
      have hT := hiff.1 h1
      rw [tangentChartMap_mk_ofVec_of_mem hφ hψ haO hT] at h2
      have : a ∈ retractTangentMap φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ.overlap ψ) (φ.transition ψ) ⁻¹' W ∩
          retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ.overlap ψ) := ⟨h2, hT⟩
      rw [hueq] at this
      refine ⟨?_, this.1⟩
      rw [hTov] at hT; exact hT.2
    · rintro ⟨h1, h2⟩
      have hT : a ∈ retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ.overlap ψ) := by
        rw [hTov]; exact ⟨haO, h1⟩
      refine ⟨hiff.2 hT, ?_⟩
      rw [tangentChartMap_mk_ofVec_of_mem hφ hψ haO hT]
      have : a ∈ u ∩ retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ.overlap ψ) := ⟨h2, hT⟩
      rw [← hueq] at this
      exact this.1

lemma tangentChart_source : (tangentChart hφ α₀).source = tangentChartSet φ := rfl

lemma tangentChart_apply (α : P.TangentSpace) : tangentChart hφ α₀ α = tangentChartMap hφ α := rfl

lemma tangentChart_model : (tangentChart hφ α₀).model = φ.model.tangent := rfl

/-- `Tφ(TV ∩ TV') = T(φ(V ∩ V'))`. -/
theorem tangentChart_overlap (hψ : P.IsChart ψ) (β₀ : P.TangentSpace) :
    (tangentChart hφ α₀).overlap (tangentChart hψ β₀) =
      retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ.overlap ψ) := by
  ext a
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨α, ⟨hα, hα'⟩, rfl⟩
    have haO := tangentChartMap_mem hφ hα
    refine (TangentPre.mem_retractTangent_image_iff inter_subset_left
      (φ.isOpen_source.inter ψ.isOpen_source) ?_).2 haO
    change φ.model.E.toBase 1 (tangentChartMap hφ α).1 ∈ φ.overlap ψ
    rw [tangentChartMap_fst hφ hα, P.toBase_levelLift hφ hα (levelVal_mem _)]
    exact ⟨_, ⟨hα, hα'⟩, rfl⟩
  · intro ha
    have haO : a ∈ retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C φ.model.O :=
      (TangentPre.mem_retractTangent_image_iff inter_subset_left
        (φ.isOpen_source.inter ψ.isOpen_source)
        (retractTangent_fst_mem (φ.isScRetract_overlap ψ) ha)).1 ha
    refine ⟨TangentSpace.mk (TangentPre.ofVec hφ haO), ⟨(TangentPre.ofVec hφ haO).mem_source, ?_⟩,
      tangentChartMap_mk_ofVec hφ haO⟩
    exact (mk_ofVec_mem_tangentChartSet_iff hφ haO).2
      (retractTangent_fst_mem (φ.isScRetract_overlap ψ) ha)

/-- **Formula (5)**: `Tψ ∘ (Tφ)⁻¹ = T(ψ ∘ φ⁻¹)` on `T(φ(V ∩ V'))`. -/
theorem tangentChart_transition (hψ : P.IsChart ψ) (β₀ : P.TangentSpace) {a : φ.model.E.tangent 0}
    (ha : a ∈ retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ.overlap ψ)) :
    (tangentChart hφ α₀).transition (tangentChart hψ β₀) a =
      retractTangentMap φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ.overlap ψ) (φ.transition ψ) a := by
  have haO : a ∈ retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C φ.model.O :=
    (TangentPre.mem_retractTangent_image_iff inter_subset_left
      (φ.isOpen_source.inter ψ.isOpen_source)
      (retractTangent_fst_mem (φ.isScRetract_overlap ψ) ha)).1 ha
  change tangentChartMap hψ (tangentChartInv hφ α₀ a) = _
  rw [tangentChartInv_of_mem hφ α₀ haO, tangentChartMap_mk_ofVec_of_mem hφ hψ haO ha]

/-- The charts `(TV, Tφ, (TO, TC, TE))` are sc-smoothly compatible (the transition maps are the
tangent maps of the sc-smooth transition maps of `X`). -/
theorem tangentChart_compatible (hψ : P.IsChart ψ) (β₀ : P.TangentSpace) :
    (tangentChart hφ α₀).Compatible (tangentChart hψ β₀) := by
  have key : ∀ (φ ψ : MChart X) (hφ : P.IsChart φ) (hψ : P.IsChart ψ) (α₀ β₀ : P.TangentSpace),
      IsScSmoothRetractMap (tangentChart hφ α₀).model.E (tangentChart hφ α₀).model.C
        ((tangentChart hφ α₀).overlap (tangentChart hψ β₀)) (tangentChart hψ β₀).model.E
        (tangentChart hψ β₀).model.C ((tangentChart hψ β₀).overlap (tangentChart hφ α₀))
        ((tangentChart hφ α₀).transition (tangentChart hψ β₀)) := by
    intro φ ψ hφ hψ α₀ β₀
    rw [tangentChart_overlap, tangentChart_overlap]
    have := (hφ.compatible hψ (P := P)).1.tangent (φ.isScRetract_overlap ψ) (ψ.isScRetract_overlap φ)
    exact this.congr fun a ha => (tangentChart_transition hφ α₀ hψ β₀ ha).symm
  exact ⟨key φ ψ hφ hψ α₀ β₀, key ψ φ hψ hφ β₀ α₀⟩

end TangentChart

/-- The atlas `(TV, Tφ, (TO, TC, TE))` of `TX`. -/
def tangentAtlas : MAtlas P.TangentSpace where
  charts := {χ | ∃ (φ : MChart X) (hφ : P.IsChart φ) (α₀ : P.TangentSpace), χ = tangentChart hφ α₀}
  compatible := by
    rintro _ ⟨φ, hφ, α₀, rfl⟩ _ ⟨ψ, hψ, β₀, rfl⟩
    exact tangentChart_compatible hφ α₀ hψ β₀
  cover α := by
    obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := TangentSpace.exists_rep α
    exact ⟨tangentChart p.isChart (TangentSpace.mk p), ⟨p.φ, p.isChart, _, rfl⟩, p.mem_source⟩

/-- **The tangent bundle `TX` as an M-polyfold** (the paragraph after Proposition 2.3.15 (preprint 2.19)).  The
paracompactness of `TX` is an instance argument, proved (Proposition 2.3.15 (preprint 2.19) (3)) by the instance
`MPolyfold.paracompactSpace_tangentSpace` in `Metrizable.lean`. -/
def tangentPolyfold [ParacompactSpace P.TangentSpace] : MPolyfold P.TangentSpace where
  atlas := P.tangentAtlas

theorem tangentPolyfold_isChart [ParacompactSpace P.TangentSpace] {φ : MChart X} (hφ : P.IsChart φ)
    (α₀ : P.TangentSpace) : P.tangentPolyfold.IsChart (tangentChart hφ α₀) :=
  P.tangentPolyfold.isChart_of_mem ⟨φ, hφ, α₀, rfl⟩

/-! ### The projection `p : TX → X¹` is sc-smooth -/

/-- The projection `TO → O₁`, `(a, h) ↦ a`, is sc-smooth between the retracts `(TO, TC, TE)` and
`(O₁, C₁, E¹)`: `pr₁ ∘ Tr = r₁ ∘ pr₁` on `TU`. -/
theorem isScSmoothRetractMap_tangent_fst {E : ScBanach} {C O : Set (E 0)} (hO : IsScRetract E C O) :
    IsScSmoothRetractMap E.tangent (E.tangentSet C) (retractTangent E C O) E.shift (E.lvlSet C 1)
      (E.lvlSet O 1) Prod.fst := by
  rw [isScSmoothRetractMap_iff_exists hO.tangentSet]
  refine ⟨fun a ha => retractTangent_fst_mem hO ha, ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨R, rfl⟩ := hO
  refine ⟨R.tangentRetraction, R.tangentRetraction_retract, ?_⟩
  have h1 : IsScSmooth (E := E.tangent) (F := E.shift) (E.tangentSet R.U) (E.tangentFst 0) :=
    E.tangentFst.isScSmooth R.isScDomain.tangentSet
  have h2 : IsScSmooth (E := E.shift) (F := E.shift) (E.lvlSet R.U 1) (levelMap R 1) :=
    R.isScSmooth.shift R.isScDomain
  exact (IsScSmooth.comp R.isScDomain.tangentSet R.isScDomain.shift h2 h1 fun _ hp => hp).congr
    R.isScDomain.tangentSet fun _ _ => rfl

/-- **`p : TX → X¹` is sc-smooth** (the paragraph after Proposition 2.3.15 (preprint 2.19)): in the charts `Tφ` of
`TX` and `φ` of `X¹` it is the projection `TO → O₁`. -/
theorem tangentProj_isScSmooth [ParacompactSpace P.TangentSpace] [ParacompactSpace (P.Level 1)] :
    P.tangentPolyfold.IsScSmoothMap P.shift P.tangentProj := by
  refine IsScSmoothOn.of_exists_charts isOpen_univ continuous_tangentProj.continuousOn fun α _ => ?_
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := TangentSpace.exists_rep α
  set φ := p.φ with hφdef
  have hφ : P.IsChart φ := p.isChart
  refine ⟨tangentChart hφ (TangentSpace.mk p), levelChart hφ (P.tangentProj (TangentSpace.mk p)),
    tangentChartSet φ, P.tangentPolyfold_isChart hφ _, P.shift_isChart hφ _, isOpen_tangentChartSet hφ,
    p.mem_source, fun β hβ => ⟨mem_univ _, hβ⟩, fun β hβ => hβ, ?_⟩
  have himg : tangentChart hφ (TangentSpace.mk p) '' tangentChartSet φ =
      retractTangent φ.model.E φ.model.C φ.model.O := (tangentChart hφ _).image_source
  rw [himg]
  refine (isScSmoothRetractMap_tangent_fst φ.model.isScRetract).congr fun a ha => ?_
  change a.1 = levelLift φ 1 (P.levelVal 1 (P.tangentProj (tangentChartInv hφ _ a)))
  rw [tangentChartInv_of_mem hφ _ ha, tangentProj_mk]
  exact (congrArg Prod.fst (TangentPre.ofVec_vec hφ ha)).symm

end MPolyfold

end Polyfold
